A||||8||Oreif||Changing Motor Mounts.||||14||
Z||000000||Oreif||05-28-2001||04:11 PM||||Well today we just changed all the motor mounts on an 87 GT with auto trans. If you plan on doing this I would suggest practicing on a chinese puzzle box prior to removing the driver side rear mount. Small hands with really long fingers would help too! Took about 4 hours to swap them all out and some "creative" pry-bar placement.<BR>(Note: colorful language helps too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  )<BR>All in all it wasn't to bad. The driver side front one was in 2 pieces so it was easy to remove. Yes, I enjoy'd the day helping a fellow Fiero fanatic fix his car.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||14
Z||000001||fiero56||05-28-2001||04:20 PM||||I just did the same job on my '86 SE v-6 4-speed last week. Both tranny mounts, engine mount, alternator, water pump, and new serp belt. I have always found on manual tranny Fieros, the front tranny mount is the biggest PITA to install. Made all the difference in the world. Shifting is much nicer(no more mucho engine movement), and no more terrible engine vibrations. Much improved.||||reg||1
Z||000002||beachbomb||05-28-2001||09:13 PM||||Hey all, i was thinking of doing the same on my 4 cyclinder, any difference between 4 and 6 cyc when replacing motor mounts, or is it better to wait until i drop the cradle one day..lmk, jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-28-2001||09:30 PM||||It all depends on your mounts. Out of all the ones we changed today, One was broken into 2 pieces. The rest were just worn. The 4-cyl with stick are easier than the auto transmissions. (More room to work with)<BR>We did it without dropping the cradle. Just a good floor jack and a 2X4 piece of wood.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||KissMySSFiero||05-28-2001||11:39 PM||||i just did the tranny mounts on my formula.  not too bad.  had to have them both out to get the rear one.  i didnt do the engine mount but i looks easy.  the key for me was get the car up high.  and be prepared to have rusty $hit fall in yoru face.  the only problem i had was the stud on the new mount busted when i over tightened.  woops.  i have to drill it out and put a bolt in there.  that sucked too.  but overall not a bad job. i also replaced the eng. strut.  now its like a rock.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||05-29-2001||01:29 AM||||I'm about to do all mounts on two of my cars... both 4 cylinders. I hear they are easier... One is my 84 Indy with 4-speed, the other is an 88 auto. I'll let you know how it goes.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Vlad||05-29-2001||02:32 AM||||I changed both auto tranny mounts on my 85 GT.<BR>The rear one was first and it was a bit?h. No space at all to titen the bolt.<BR>The front one was really easy and it took less than an hour. With a help of second person I could have done it in 30 minutes.<BR>Tools required: 15 mm deep socket, 15 mm wrench and jack.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroJoe||05-29-2001||10:27 AM||||How many are there on my 87 4 cyl 5spd?  I have replaced the dogbone and it did tighten up a little bit, but I think from high mileage (220k) and a worn dogbone the engine and tranny mounts could probably be replaced.  Are there 2 engine and 2 tranny mounts?  What do you recommend, rubber or poly?  This is my daily driver, if that makes any difference, and the dogbone is the ultimate dogbone.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||05-29-2001||10:47 AM||||There are 2 trans mounts. (One right side and one left side) and 2 engine mounts. (One at the front of the engine and the dog bone) On V-6's there is a small mount on the left side That looks like a miniature shock absorber. As far as I know you can't get these anymore.<P>(NOTE: right side = rear of car<BR>Left side = front of car) ||||reg||1
